  "description": "Author-hosted lecture notes for the Oxford course C3.3b Differentiable Manifolds (2014 version, 94 PDF pages): coordinate charts and the definition of a manifold, maps between manifolds, tangent and cotangent vectors, vector fields and flows, tensor products and the exterior algebra, differential forms, partitions of unity, the exterior derivative, de Rham cohomology, integration and Stokes' theorem, the degree of a map, a short chapter on Riemannian metrics and the geodesic flow, and an appendix of technical results (inverse function theorem, ODE existence, partitions of unity, a special case of Sard's theorem).",
